  "body": "Part of #3663 (the tool library dialog). Step U9: the tool list. After U8 (the dialog frame). Search uses the part number and vendor fields of #898 when they exist.\n\n## What happens\n\n![tool list: mockup left, current right](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/qsmits/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/toollib-compare/1-tool-list.png)\n\n- The top of the list is a stack of controls over about 280 px: the file buttons, \"Import tool holders\", the source tabs, a type combo and a \"Name filter\" box with a label above it.\n- The filter matches the tool name only.\n- The category rail shows only groups that have tools. There is no Recipes column and no \"in document\" mark.\n\n## Expected (mockup)\n\n- One compact header row: the source tabs (Document, My library, Catalog), one search box, and **New tool**, **Import**, **Export**.\n- **Search:** one box with the placeholder \"Filter by name, diameter or part number\". It matches the name, the type, the cutting diameter, the shank diameter, the holder and the tool number together (\"6 ball\" finds the 6 mm ball nose mills). After #898 it also matches the part number and the vendor. It works the same in Document, My library and Catalog. The list shows \"N of M tools\". Esc clears the box.\n- The category rail lists all groups, with a count for each.\n- Columns: T, Name, Type, Ø, Flute, Flutes, Holder, Gauge, **Recipes** (count), and an **in document** mark for library and catalog rows.\n- The footer hint \"Click a row to edit the tool.\"\n\n## Done means\n\n- Tests for the search (one term, two terms, a diameter, no match, Esc) in each source.\n- `layout_page_tool_library` asserts the header row, the columns and the result count.\n- Before and after screenshots in the PR body.\n\nEffort: medium (one page and its tests).\n",
